---
import type { ModelGuide } from '../data/rickenbacker-models';
import { rickenbackerGuideSlug } from '../data/rickenbacker-models';
import { rickenbackerPhotoSets } from '../data/rickenbacker-model-photos';
import LicensedImage from './primitives/LicensedImage.astro';
import RickenbackerPhoto from './RickenbackerPhoto.astro';
import RickenbackerValueTable from './RickenbackerValueTable.astro';
import { resolveImage } from '../lib/images';
import '../styles/rickenbacker-models.css';
interface Props { model:ModelGuide; kind:'authentication'|'value' }
const {model:m,kind}=Astro.props;
const auth=kind==='authentication';
const photos=rickenbackerPhotoSets[m.photoSet];
const hero=resolveImage(photos[0].file);
if(!hero)throw new Error(`Missing model hero: ${m.key}`);
const sections=auth?m.authentication:m.valuation;
const counterpart=auth?'value':'authentication';
const topics=[...(!auth?[{id:'prices',label:'2026 Value Chart'}]:[]),{id:'model',label:'Models And Variants'},...sections.map((s,i)=>({id:`detail-${i+1}`,label:s.heading})),{id:'inspection',label:auth?'Authentication Checklist':'From Market Value To An Offer'},{id:'photos',label:'Photos For An Appraisal'},{id:'sources',label:auth?'Sources And Further Reading':'Related Rickenbacker Guides'}];
---
<div class="ric-model">
 <nav class="ric-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/blog/">Blog</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/rickenbacker-authentication-and-value-guides/">Rickenbacker Guides</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span>{auth?'Authentication':'Value'}</span></nav>
 <article>
  <header class="ric-hero">
   <div class="ric-hero-copy"><p class="ric-eyebrow">{m.group} · {m.period}</p><h1>Rickenbacker {m.name}<span>{auth?'Authentication Guide':'Value Guide'}</span></h1><p class="ric-lede">{auth?m.intro:`What is a Rickenbacker ${m.name.toLowerCase()} worth? Use Joe’s 2026 value chart for estimated market ranges in US dollars, organized by model, production years and configuration. Then check the condition and originality details that affect your instrument.`}</p><p class="ric-byline">By <a href="/about-me/">Joe Dampt</a> · Updated <time datetime={auth?"2026-10-27":"2026-10-29"}>{auth?"October 27, 2026":"October 29, 2026"}</time></p><div class="ric-actions"><a class="ric-button" href="/free-appraisal/">Get A Free Appraisal</a><a href={`/post/${rickenbackerGuideSlug(m,counterpart)}/`}>Read The {auth?'Value':'Authentication'} Guide</a></div></div>
   <figure class="ric-hero-photo"><LicensedImage src={hero} alt={photos[0].alt} caption={photos[0].caption} width={1200} loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" sizes="(max-width: 850px) 100vw, 50vw" /><figcaption>{photos[0].caption}</figcaption></figure>
  </header>
  <div class="ric-layout"><aside><details class="ric-contents" open><summary>In This Guide</summary><nav aria-label="On This Page"><ol>{topics.map(t=><li><a href={`#${t.id}`}>{t.label}</a></li>)}</ol></nav></details><a class="ric-library-link" href="/rickenbacker-authentication-and-value-guides/">Browse All Rickenbacker Models</a></aside>
   <div class="ric-body">
    {!auth && <RickenbackerValueTable modelKey={m.key} name={m.name}/>}
    <p class="ric-photo-note"><strong>About These Photos</strong>{m.comparison} Click a detail photograph to enlarge it.</p>
    <section id="model"><p class="ric-eyebrow">Identify Before You Compare</p><h2>Models And Variants</h2><dl class="ric-variants">{m.variants.map(([term,description])=><div><dt>{term}</dt><dd>{description}</dd></div>)}</dl></section>

    {sections.map((s,i)=><section id={`detail-${i+1}`}><h2>{s.heading}</h2>{s.paragraphs.map(p=><p>{p}</p>)}<div class="ric-photo-grid">{photos.slice(1+i*2,3+i*2).map(p=><RickenbackerPhoto {...p}/>)}</div></section>)}
    <section id="inspection"><h2>{auth?'Authentication Checklist':'From Market Value To An Offer'}</h2>{auth?<><p>Keep four questions separate: is it a Rickenbacker, is the model correctly identified, is the date supported, and which parts or finishes remain original? A positive answer to one does not settle the others.</p><ol class="ric-checklist"><li><strong>Record the identity.</strong> Save the complete serial photograph, model claim, measurements and any dated paperwork. Use the <a href="/rickenbacker-serial-numbers/">serial lookup</a> only for the formats it covers.</li><li><strong>Compare independent details.</strong> Check body construction, neck, pickups, tuners and controls against the same model and period. One replaced part may explain a mismatch; several unexplained conflicts need closer inspection.</li><li><strong>Describe condition precisely.</strong> Separate wear, refret, replacement nut, repaired breaks, routing, touch-up, overspray and refinishing. See <a href="/how-to-tell-if-a-guitar-has-been-refinished/">our photo guide to refinishing clues</a>.</li><li><strong>Inspect internally when justified.</strong> Have a qualified repairer document hidden routes, wiring and component dates if a disputed claim affects the purchase. Do not force old screws, fragile guards or an unfamiliar neck adjustment.</li><li><strong>Keep uncertainty visible.</strong> “Consistent with this period” is different from a proven exact date or a claim that every solder joint is untouched. Photos can guide an appraisal; some findings require an in-person examination.</li></ol></>:<><p>Start with the chart row for the correct model, years and configuration. The ranges describe estimated market value for excellent, original instruments. A direct purchase offer also accounts for condition, needed work and the time involved in preparing the instrument for its next owner.</p><ol class="ric-checklist"><li><strong>Confirm the model and year.</strong> Use the matching authentication guide and document the serial, construction and original configuration. Do not apply a rare-variant range before confirming that identity.</li><li><strong>Account for known work.</strong> Get a specific repair estimate. Do not apply a universal percentage for every refinish, neck repair or changed pickup. See <a href="/what-lowers-vintage-guitar-value/">the changes that affect vintage guitar value</a>.</li><li><strong>Estimate your net proceeds.</strong> For a private sale, subtract actual selling fees, shipping, insurance and agreed repairs from the expected selling price. A hypothetical $4,000 sale with $400 in total costs would net $3,600; those figures illustrate arithmetic, not a fee schedule or this model’s value.</li><li><strong>Compare the complete offer.</strong> Include who handles packing, payment, shipping and any repairs. A direct purchase offer should be assessed on its terms and certainty as well as the dollar amount.</li></ol><p>Use the <a href={`/post/${rickenbackerGuideSlug(m,'authentication')}/`}>matching authentication guide</a> before assigning a premium for originality or an unusual version.</p></>}</section>
    <section id="photos"><h2>Photos For An Appraisal</h2><p>Take unfiltered photographs in even light. Include the full front and back, both headstock faces, the entire serial or other markings, pickups, controls, bridge, neck joint and any damage. Add the measurements or model-specific views described above. Photograph the case, paperwork and removed parts separately.</p><p>You do not need to take the instrument apart for an initial review. If a detail cannot be seen, say so. A clear statement of known repairs and unknown history is more useful than an unsupported claim of complete originality.</p>{photos.length>(auth?9:7) && <div class="ric-photo-grid">{photos.slice(auth?9:7).map(p=><RickenbackerPhoto {...p}/>)}</div>}<div class="ric-appraisal"><h3>Have A Rickenbacker To Identify Or Sell?</h3><p>Send Joe your photos and any known history. We can help identify the instrument, discuss its condition and make an offer if you are ready to sell.</p><div class="ric-actions"><a class="ric-button" href="/free-appraisal/">Send Photos For An Appraisal</a><a href="/sell-my-rickenbacker-guitar/">Sell My Rickenbacker</a></div></div></section>
    <section id="sources"><h2>{auth?'Sources And Further Reading':'Related Rickenbacker Guides'}</h2>{auth && <><p>Factory documents establish period model descriptions. Instrument-specific references help compare construction; their originality claims are not independent certifications.</p><ul class="ric-sources">{m.sources.map(s=><li><a href={s.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{s.title}</a><span>{s.note}</span></li>)}</ul></>}<nav class="ric-resource-links" aria-label="Rickenbacker Detail Guides"><a href="/rickenbacker-serial-numbers/">Serial Numbers</a><a href="/rickenbacker-pickup-dating-guide/">Pickups</a><a href="/rickenbacker-tuner-dating-guide/">Tuners</a><a href="/rickenbacker-knobs-and-controls/">Controls</a><a href="/rickenbacker-body-binding-and-inlays/">Body And Inlays</a><a href="/rickenbacker-tailpiece-dating-guide/">Tailpieces</a><a href="/rickenbacker-finish-colors/">Finish Colors</a></nav></section>
    <details class="ric-credits"><summary>Photo Credits And Scope</summary><p>Photographs are from Joe’s Vintage Guitars’ instrument archive. Captions identify the actual instrument shown, including related-model and later-production comparisons. Full frames and existing watermarks are retained. A photograph of another model is not evidence of the correct construction for yours.</p></details>
    <nav class="ric-pair-nav" aria-label="Related Model Guides"><a href={`/post/${rickenbackerGuideSlug(m,counterpart)}/`}>Rickenbacker {m.name}: {auth?'Value':'Authentication'} Guide</a><a href="/rickenbacker-authentication-and-value-guides/">All Rickenbacker Model Guides</a></nav>
   </div>
  </div>
 </article>
</div>
